WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Why does Paul call grace a gift?

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:06.920
Think about a paycheck.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.480
You worked for it,

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.860
so your employer owes you those wages.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.460
In Romans four,

6
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.420
Paul uses that contrast to explain righteousness

7
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.340
before God.

8
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.200
A wage is earned.

9
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.240
A gift is received.

10
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.560
God justifies the ungodly who trust him.

11
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.420
Faith receives what God gives through Christ;

12
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.460
it does not put God in our

13
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:28.720
debt.

14
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.340
That gift came through the redemption that

15
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.620
is in Christ Jesus.

16
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.220
Grace is free to us because Christ

17
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.020
paid the cost.

18
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.620
As you read Romans,

19
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.120
notice where Paul excludes boasting.

20
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.100
Then thank God for the righteousness you

21
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.040
could never earn.
